1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,586
Every week I get at least three emails

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:06,506
from districts all over the state of California

3
00:00:06,506 --> 00:00:08,466
looking for theater teachers.

4
00:00:08,466 --> 00:00:11,594
It's a great time to be a theater teacher.

5
00:00:11,594 --> 00:00:14,222
In order to get into
a credential program,

6
00:00:14,222 --> 00:00:16,891
you need to meet the following requirements.

7
00:00:16,891 --> 00:00:19,519
First, you need a bachelor's degree.

8
00:00:19,519 --> 00:00:21,396
Second, you need to show

9
00:00:21,396 --> 00:00:23,648
subject matter competency.

10
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:26,693
Subject matter competency simply means

11
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:28,945
that you know your stuff about theater.

12
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:31,364
This is because
a credential program doesn't

13
00:00:31,364 --> 00:00:32,907
teach you what to teach,

14
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:35,744
it teaches you
how to teach what you know.

15
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:37,454
Most applicants already

16
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:38,747
have an undergraduate

17
00:00:38,747 --> 00:00:40,582
or graduate theater degree,

18
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:41,875
which is all you need for

19
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:43,626
subject matter competency.

20
00:00:43,668 --> 00:00:47,047
Most people who don't have subject matter competency

21
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:48,465
through a degree

22
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:52,135
go through a process called transcript evaluation.

23
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:55,722
This means that you complete a form and somebody - 

24
00:00:55,722 --> 00:00:57,682
at Cal State East Bay, me -

25
00:00:57,932 --> 00:01:00,143
looks at your transcripts
and determines

26
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:01,352
if you have the knowledge

27
00:01:01,352 --> 00:01:03,229
and skills to teach theater.

28
00:01:03,313 --> 00:01:05,106
This almost always fulfills

29
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:06,983
subject matter competency,

30
00:01:07,025 --> 00:01:10,028
especially if you have a theater or a drama minor.

31
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:11,529
If you don't have a degree,

32
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:14,157
you can always take the CSET exam.

33
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:15,742
Professional experience

34
00:01:15,742 --> 00:01:17,243
and classes taken outside

35
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:18,536
of higher education

36
00:01:18,536 --> 00:01:19,996
do not count towards

37
00:01:19,996 --> 00:01:21,956
subject matter competency.

38
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:24,250
And although
many of our students

39
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:25,752
have lots of experience

40
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:27,003
working with kids,

41
00:01:27,003 --> 00:01:28,338
teaching experience

42
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:29,839
is not a requirement

43
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:31,758
to get into the program.

44
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,176
Remember, it's our job

45
00:01:33,176 --> 00:01:34,886
to teach you how to teach.

46
00:01:35,136 --> 00:01:37,472
What is important
is that you have

47
00:01:37,472 --> 00:01:40,058
the dispositions
to be a good teacher,

48
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:41,518
such as an understanding

49
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:42,977
of collaboration,

50
00:01:43,061 --> 00:01:45,271
the habit of self-reflection,

51
00:01:45,396 --> 00:01:46,981
the belief that all students

52
00:01:46,981 --> 00:01:49,067
have the ability to learn.

53
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:52,028
The willingness to take on responsibilities

54
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:55,490
and a commitment to ongoing learning.
